# End-to-End Bearing Fault Predictive Maintenance System

An industrial-grade predictive maintenance pipeline for drive-end bearing fault diagnostics using 48 kHz vibration signals from the Case Western Reserve University (CWRU) dataset.

## Key Features & Engineering Rigor
- **Leak-Free Signal Segmentation:** 2,048-sample sliding windowing (50% overlap) grouped via `GroupShuffleSplit` across contiguous 10-window blocks to eliminate temporal data leakage.
- **14 Diagnostic Features:** 
  - *Time-Domain:* RMS, Kurtosis, Skewness, Crest Factor, Form Factor, Max, Min, Mean, Std Dev.
  - *Frequency-Domain:* Spectral Centroid, Spectral Spread, Peak Frequency, Low/High Spectral Energies via Hann-windowed RFFT.
- **Imbalance Mitigation:** Simulates real-world factory fault rarity (10:1 normal-to-fault ratio) using class-weighted Random Forest classification.
- **Explainability & Web Dashboard:** SHAP feature importance analysis paired with an interactive Streamlit diagnostic dashboard.

